{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.VandermondeUpdateRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.VandermondeUpdateRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.LagrangeCoeffSum"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_vandPairProd_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_vandPairProd_scale","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/VandermondeUpdateRatio.lean#L171-L197","doc":"**Branching, unconditionally, for the Vandermonde pair product.**\n\n`∑_{a<n} V(x[a ↦ Q·x_a]) = (1 + Q + ⋯ + Q^{n−1}) · V(x)`.\n\nScaling node `a` by `Q` is what adding a box to row `a` does to the shifted parts\n`x_i = Q^{μ_i + r − i}`; `vandPairProd_update_div` turns each summand into the `a`-th `q`-ratio and\n`QOU.Mathlib.sum_prod_qratio` sums those to `[n]_Q`.\n\nRows to which a box cannot be added need no separate treatment: there `Q·x_a = x_{a−1}`, so the\nupdated node collides with its neighbour and `V` vanishes — `vandPairProd_update_eq_zero` below.\nSumming over all rows and summing over addable rows are therefore the same sum, which is what the\n`r = 2` chain needed `rowLen_two_addCell_row2` for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd_update_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd_update_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/VandermondeUpdateRatio.lean#L156-L167","doc":"**A collided node kills the product.**\n\nIf the updated value equals the node just above it, the pair `(a−1, a)` contributes a zero factor.\nApplied to a partition: adding a box to row `a` is illegal exactly when `μ_a = μ_{a−1}`, and then the\nshifted parts satisfy `β_{a−1} = β_a + 1`, i.e. `x_{a−1} = Q·x_a`.  So the illegal rows contribute\nnothing to the sum in `sum_vandPairProd_scale` and need no separate case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd_update_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd_update_div","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/VandermondeUpdateRatio.lean#L145-L154","doc":"The ratio form, over a field: `V(x[a ↦ y]) / V(x) = ∏_{j ≠ a} (y − x_j)/(x_a − x_j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd_update","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd_update","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/VandermondeUpdateRatio.lean#L83-L143","doc":"**Scaling one node of the Vandermonde pair product, division-free.**\n\n`V(x[a ↦ y]) · ∏_{j ≠ a}(x_a − x_j) = ∏_{j ≠ a}(y − x_j) · V(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.inner_prod_update","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.inner_prod_update","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/VandermondeUpdateRatio.lean#L62-L81","doc":"Row `i ≠ a` of the double product, under a single-node update.  The updated node shows up as the\nsingle factor `x i − y` when `i < a`, and not at all when `i > a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.prod_erase_range_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.prod_erase_range_split","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/VandermondeUpdateRatio.lean#L47-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.vandPairProd","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/VandermondeUpdateRatio.lean#L43-L45","doc":"`∏_{i<j<n} (x i − x j)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}